Certificate Issurance:
- Wildcard certificates: *.mydomain.com, with this we can install one certificate on multiple websites ending with mydomain.com.
- Extended domain validation: enhanced CA due diligence against certificare requester like valid company name or not etc..
- Code signing certificates to digitally sign code

PKI Certificate life cycle:
Certificate signing request -> Issuance -> Use -> Revocation -> renewal/expiry

Certificate Templates:
- pre-defined templates used to issue certificates
- they utilize encryption and signing algorithms
- they use certificate usage constraints

### Creating an AWS KMS key
- AWS Managed keys: These are created and managed by AWS. they gets created automatically when any new AWS service created and attched to respective service.
- Customer managed keys: We can create and manage keys under this section
- Asymmetric key creation has two key usage options:
  - encrypt and decrypt: use the key only to encrypt and decrypt data
  - sign and verify: key pairs for digital signing. use the private key for signing and public key for verification (specs like RSA_2048, RSA_4096 etc used for signing and verification)

